※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=-4 diag=none

※ An answer that will not fit stops the program and says so.  It dies by a
※ signal at the point of the fault, with its stack still standing, which is
※ what a debugger wants to be handed; the message has already been written by
※ the time the signal arrives.  Four is SIGILL, which every target raises.

let two_hundred: u8 = 200u8
let one_hundred: u8 = 100u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    two_hundred + one_hundred
